WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.528
Every state, including Maryland, adopted a model law listing provisions that

00:00:04.528 --> 00:00:08.645
individual health policies must contain and others they may contain.

00:00:08.645 --> 00:00:13.173
The required provisions protect the insured and may be worded differently

00:00:13.173 --> 00:00:17.290
only if the insurer’s version is at least as favorable.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:22.642
Rosa’s disability policy and Marcus’s individual medical plan therefore share the same skeleton.

00:00:22.642 --> 00:00:27.993
This lesson covers the provisions about the contract and the premium; Lesson 16

00:00:27.993 --> 00:00:32.933
covers the claim clocks; Lesson 17 covers the optional provisions and renewability.

00:00:32.933 --> 00:00:36.227
The exam tests these as day counts and

00:00:36.227 --> 00:00:39.520
rules, so learn each number with its purpose.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:42.948
The entire contract provision states that the policy, including any

00:00:42.948 --> 00:00:46.033
endorsements and the attached application, is the whole agreement.

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:49.461
Nothing said outside those documents is part of the contract.

00:00:49.461 --> 00:00:52.546
No statement by the applicant can be used against

00:00:52.546 --> 00:00:55.288
her unless it is in the attached application.

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:59.401
Changes to the policy are valid only if approved by an executive

00:00:59.401 --> 00:01:03.514
officer of the insurer and endorsed on or attached to the policy.

00:01:03.514 --> 00:01:07.628
A producer cannot change the policy or waive any of its provisions.

00:01:07.628 --> 00:01:12.084
If Theo promises Rosa a benefit the policy does not contain, the promise

00:01:12.084 --> 00:01:16.540
is not part of the contract, and he has exposed himself to liability.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:20.953
After the policy has been in force for two years, the

00:01:20.953 --> 00:01:25.366
insurer may no longer use misstatements in the application, other than

00:01:25.366 --> 00:01:29.378
fraudulent ones, to void the policy or deny a claim.

00:01:29.378 --> 00:01:34.193
It also may not deny a claim after those two years by

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:38.606
calling a condition pre-existing unless the policy excluded it by name.

00:01:38.606 --> 00:01:43.420
This is the health insurance counterpart to the life insurance incontestability clause.

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:46.630
Rosa’s innocent error about a past prescription cannot

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:49.438
be raised against her in year three.

00:01:49.438 --> 00:01:53.049
Deliberate fraud remains contestable, and some policies use the

00:01:53.049 --> 00:01:56.660
stricter incontestable wording that drops even the fraud exception.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:59.211
A grace period gives the insured time to

00:01:59.211 --> 00:02:01.443
pay a late premium while coverage continues.

00:02:01.443 --> 00:02:04.631
The uniform provision requires at least seven days for weekly

00:02:04.631 --> 00:02:07.820
premium policies, ten days for monthly premium policies and thirty-one

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:11.008
days for all other modes, such as quarterly or annual.

00:02:11.008 --> 00:02:13.559
A claim during the grace period is paid,

00:02:13.559 --> 00:02:16.110
although the insurer may deduct the overdue premium.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:19.298
If the premium is still unpaid when the grace period

00:02:19.298 --> 00:02:22.168
ends, the policy lapses as of the due date.

00:02:22.168 --> 00:02:25.994
Marcus pays monthly, so a premium due on the first is late

00:02:25.994 --> 00:02:29.820
on the eleventh, and his policy lapses if nothing arrives by then.

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:32.577
A lapsed policy can come back.

00:02:32.577 --> 00:02:37.630
If the insurer accepts a late premium without requiring a reinstatement

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:42.224
application, the policy is reinstated when the premium is accepted.

00:02:42.224 --> 00:02:47.278
If the insurer requires an application and issues a conditional receipt

00:02:47.278 --> 00:02:52.331
for the premium, the policy is reinstated when the insurer approves

00:02:52.331 --> 00:02:57.385
the application, or automatically on the forty-fifth day after the receipt

00:02:57.385 --> 00:03:01.979
date if the insurer has not disapproved it in writing.

00:03:01.979 --> 00:03:06.573
A reinstated policy covers accidents immediately but covers sickness only

00:03:06.573 --> 00:03:10.708
if it begins more than ten days after reinstatement.

00:03:10.708 --> 00:03:17.140
The insurer and insured otherwise have the same rights they had before the lapse.

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:17.765
Follow Marcus.

00:03:17.765 --> 00:03:20.891
His monthly premium is due June 1 and he forgets.

00:03:20.891 --> 00:03:24.018
Through June 10 he is in the grace period; a

00:03:24.018 --> 00:03:26.831
June 7 injury is covered, less the overdue premium.

00:03:26.831 --> 00:03:29.957
On June 11 the policy lapses back to June 1.

00:03:29.957 --> 00:03:32.458
On July 20 he sends the premium with

00:03:32.458 --> 00:03:34.959
a reinstatement application and gets a conditional receipt.

00:03:34.959 --> 00:03:36.210
The insurer says nothing.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:39.961
On the forty-fifth day after July 20 the policy is reinstated automatically.

00:03:39.961 --> 00:03:44.025
An accident the next morning is covered; a sickness that begins three days

00:03:44.025 --> 00:03:48.089
later is not, because sickness must start more than ten days after reinstatement.

00:03:48.089 --> 00:03:50.590
Every step is a number from this lesson.
